    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nOn successful owner creation, the `POST /api/owners` pipeline now emits an audit line to the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Reads the persisted `@Val Owner` and logs to `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")` a line carrying the owner **id**, **customerCode**, and **registrationDate**.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step (under `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `save` and `respond`, so the id assigned during `save` is present in the audit record.\n\nThe audit step runs only after all validation/quota checks and the save succeed, so the line is emitted exactly on a successful create. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), and the observed log line confirms the format, e.g. `AUDIT - owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-07`.",
